---
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
import Answer from "../../components/challenge/Answer.astro";
import ChallengeIntro from "../../components/challenge/ChallengeIntro.astro";
import Checklist from "../../components/challenge/Checklist.astro";
import Message from "../../components/challenge/Message.astro";
import Task from "../../components/challenge/Task.astro";
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Sizzle Video - AI Training Guide">
	<PageShell chapterId="exploring-ai-capabilities" subChapterId="sizzle-video">
		<ChallengeIntro skill="The agent can make polished work well outside everyday code, like a video, when you give it clear creative direction: length, beats, tone, references and where to get footage.">
			Marketing needs a short launch video for instant quotes. You'll direct the agent to build it with Remotion, a library that
			makes videos from React, using footage recorded from the real website.
		</ChallengeIntro>

		<Message kind="email" subject="Launch video for instant quotes" from="Marketing" to="Web Team" date="Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:20">
			<p>
				We're launching instant quotes: a real price on the spot, from any page on the website. We need a 25-second video for the
				launch.
			</p>
			<p>It should look like a serious company launching a serious product, because we are one.</p>
		</Message>

		<Task>Write a prompt to have your agent make a 25-second launch video from real footage of the website using Remotion. Give it some direction on the style and content of the video.</Task>

		<Checklist
			items={[
				"Set up the video project in its own folder, outside the apps.",
				"Record real footage: the 3D city from the home page, and the quote modal being filled in.",
				"End the footage on the price appearing.",
				"Use the website's colors and typeface, and keep its calm, straight-faced tone.",
				'End on the line "Kaiju Mutual. A price before landfall."',
				"Render an MP4 between 20 and 30 seconds long.",
			]}
		/>

		<Callout variant="info" title="Before you start">
			<p>
				Recording the screen with agent-browser needs ffmpeg, which isn't in the project's prerequisites. Install it with{" "}
				<code>brew install ffmpeg</code>, or let the agent tell you when it needs it.
			</p>
		</Callout>

		<Answer
			prompt={`Using Remotion, make a 25-second launch video for our instant quotes. Set it up in its own folder, not in the apps.

Open on the 3D city from the home page (record it with agent-browser), cut to the Get a quote modal being filled in, and land on the price appearing. Three or four beats, big type, our brand colors and font from the website. The tone is calm and straight-faced, like the site: an insurer, not a monster movie. Make it feel like an Anthropic launch video. End on "Kaiju Mutual. A price before landfall." Render it to MP4.`}
		>
			<p>
				Try a one-line prompt first, such as "make a launch video for instant quotes", then the detailed one. A vague prompt gets
				a generic video. The skill is in the direction.
			</p>
			<p>
				An agent that skips recording produces motion graphics with no real UI. Check that the city and the quote modal are real
				footage from the running website.
			</p>
			<p>
				The colors and typeface live in the website's <code>app.css</code>. A good agent reads them from there instead of
				guessing from screenshots.
			</p>
		</Answer>
	</PageShell>
</MainLayout>
